<p></p>
<p><br></p>
<h1 id=3D"PRDUnifiedNavigation(deeplinkingR2featuresinCX)-FeaturePositionin=
g">Feature Positioning</h1>
<h2 id=3D"PRDUnifiedNavigation(deeplinkingR2featuresinCX)-FeatureOverview">=
Feature Overview</h2>
<p>The primary objective of our initiative is to decommission legacy platfo=
rms and move all features to CX. However, the rebuild of all these features=
 is expected to continue till next year and in the mean time we want to add=
ress the user challenges of navigation between multiple platforms by provid=
ing a unified navigation experience in CX which will also support all futur=
e feature rebuilds (for deep linked features)</p>
<h2 id=3D"PRDUnifiedNavigation(deeplinkingR2featuresinCX)-ProblemStatement"=
>Problem Statement</h2>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"6a49dc71-8640-47c6-81fb-08ec4a47704e">Clients are unable =
to identify whether Compass feature is available on CX or R2</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"6ccde9b0-4c0c-49b1-a0b9-53dc7dacb39b">Clients find it tim=
e consuming and inefficient to navigate between multiple platforms to compl=
ete their tasks</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"fba7690d-1e1d-4920-8edd-45df16a46a73">Clients are burdene=
d with multiple navigation workflows that exist today and move to legacy fo=
r completing their tasks</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"85cdd6fc-3240-488a-b806-61860e950de7">Clients want access=
 to full feature functionality in one platform in order to complete their t=
asks</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"fbad3e61-3a8d-4ba7-9e32-357f863ca9af">Client communicatio=
n, client training, feature onboarding and setting up access to new feature=
s is high effort activity as new feature launches are scattered across quar=
ters</li>
</ul>
<h2 id=3D"PRDUnifiedNavigation(deeplinkingR2featuresinCX)-BenefitsHypothesi=
s">Benefits Hypothesis</h2>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"11ac4c01-f663-4f6f-8c2d-7c3b4c61c44a">User Experience - R=
educe the number of clicks and burden on users to navigate to correct platf=
orm for accessing a particular feature</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"266e053f-88a4-4052-aa83-6a87a941509c">CX Adoption - Elimi=
nate the need for users to navigate to legacy platforms&nbsp;</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"ea0c5f8e-01cf-43dc-85b7-6f2215141b3e">Operational Efficie=
ncy :&nbsp;One time effort for feature onboarding and client communication<=
/li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"3daa22b8-e223-49bf-98da-cdb68c4a7caf">Security Vulnerabil=
ities : Enabling unified navigation would allow us to address the security =
vulnerabilities related to direct R2 access by users</li>
</ul>
<h2 id=3D"PRDUnifiedNavigation(deeplinkingR2featuresinCX)-TargetAudience">T=
arget Audience</h2>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"c4fc9a18-ca21-425f-91d2-11bdcae72702">All CX users</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"0e51b9ad-772b-4e63-b48e-8f3ae5ca0a59">NBIN teams - F&amp;=
UM, Product Activations &amp; Product Support</li>
</ul>
<h2 id=3D"PRDUnifiedNavigation(deeplinkingR2featuresinCX)-FeatureObjectives=
&amp;Metrics">Feature Objectives &amp; Metrics</h2>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"daf56678-6a71-4932-a4b7-9de7b142beda">
  <p>Enable unified navigation in CX for features available in - R1/R2</p><=
/li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"f3b7c1a1-2613-4c28-995a-4c1a83e18eec">Enable unified navi=
gation which adapts to feature access and permissions while also supports t=
he long term vision of rebuilding of these features.&nbsp;</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"754e58a5-649a-4cda-9314-f1ebcfea6990">
  <p>Enable unified navigation for all user types - single firm user, multi=
 firm user</p>
  <ul>
   <li data-uuid=3D"448b6356-7a5a-43c7-b455-f7ddefb3d7e0">
    <p><em><strong>TBD - When will multi firm user be available in CX? ; Sh=
ould deep linking be prioritized before multi-firm user feature is availabl=
e in CX and what should our feature objectives with regards to this point?<=
/strong></em></p></li>
   <li data-uuid=3D"068c4bb5-d08e-40f9-9065-e8da769489e9"><em><strong>TBD -=
 When will unified CX/R2 Access or User Profile be available in CX ? Should=
 deep linking be prioritized before unified access and what should be our f=
eature objectives with regards to this point ?</strong></em></li>
  </ul></li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"fe47535a-a8b1-4096-ae46-69a1d77bc10b">
  <p>Enable unified navigation for all feature types - standalone or permis=
sion driven or context preservation</p></li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"7cdf2a4c-3a60-45d9-9ef1-5223f39b9649">
  <p>Unified navigation should achieve disabling the Compass Legacy navigat=
ion link in CX and disabling navigation within R2 itself for firm users</p>
  <ul>
   <li style=3D"font-weight: bold;font-style: italic;" data-uuid=3D"0f8c49e=
d-c7ce-4fdd-a4a9-30651bda6d61">
    <p><em><strong>TBD - Are there any other scenarios which need to be con=
sidered?&nbsp;</strong></em>&nbsp;</p></li>
  </ul></li>
</ul>
<h1 id=3D"PRDUnifiedNavigation(deeplinkingR2featuresinCX)-FeatureScope">Fea=
ture Scope</h1>
<h2 id=3D"PRDUnifiedNavigation(deeplinkingR2featuresinCX)-InScope">In Scope=
</h2>
<p>Following features in scope for deeplinking:&nbsp;<a class=3D"external-l=
ink" href=3D"https://nbin.aha.io/bookmarks/custom_pivots/763456833961792880=
8" rel=3D"nofollow">https://nbin.aha.io/bookmarks/custom_pivots/76345683396=
17928808</a></p>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"32452198-c537-4c74-b294-68d70c7d1da1">Identified feature =
types:&nbsp;=20
  <ul>
   <li>ResoureLibrary - <span>User engages, inputs parameters to view and d=
ownload content from Compass ie. PDF files&nbsp;</span></li>
   <li>PlatformUtility - common platform services</li>
   <li>ClientLifecycleManagement - <span>non transaction request ie. accoun=
t updates</span></li>
   <li>Integration - external applications</li>
   <li>Feature - front-end client facing functionality</li>
   <li>Service - APIs and back-end service, etc.</li>
   <li>Other - activity type items and/or F&amp;UM and/or need further revi=
ew</li>
  </ul></li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"1d3feeb1-29a6-4e1b-9a82-dc4a8ab93543">Identified deeplink=
 patterns:=20
  <ul>
   <li>Not required - will not be migrated over</li>
   <li>Cannot deep link - too complex or need to be rebuilt or cannot be de=
ep linked</li>
   <li>Permission driven - based on rr range or role</li>
   <li>Context - combination of rr/role, account and client id</li>
   <li>Standalone - no context, all users have access to the same functiona=
lity</li>
  </ul></li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"6e856ecc-35bb-4840-be64-e2bb9c60345f">Prioritized based o=
n deeplink pattern as follows:&nbsp;=20
  <ul>
   <li>Permission Passing - prioritizing as likely, requested features</li>
   <li>Context Passing&nbsp;</li>
   <li>Standalone - easiest but anticipated low usage and therefore low pri=
ority</li>
  </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2 style=3D"text-align: left;" id=3D"PRDUnifiedNavigation(deeplinkingR2fea=
turesinCX)-OutofScope">Out of Scope</h2>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"6ba592c5-d175-430b-9ae3-44017afcfe1b">Rebuilding UI for d=
eep linked feature</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"31b8a035-ec2f-4860-b84a-ffdc374cf0f3">Rebuilding backend =
services for deep linked feature</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"9f9e528e-0e6e-4f36-a705-afc5b2852c8d">Disable R2 login pa=
ge <em><strong>(TBD - should this be a Unified Navigation objective?)</stro=
ng></em></li>
</ul>
<h2 style=3D"text-align: left;" id=3D"PRDUnifiedNavigation(deeplinkingR2fea=
turesinCX)-KeyAssumptions">Key Assumptions</h2>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"057bfc63-8c9a-4235-be68-09510418e540">Context passing dur=
ing deep linking is feasible.&nbsp;</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"32404f89-e066-4698-a366-5cbdb29ce0df">Existing setup, pro=
cesses and request queues will work for deep linked features.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"ee16091c-cdd7-4519-9792-1d40136bd089">Deep linking can be=
 implemented fairly quickly and is low effort for discovery and implementat=
ion both.</li>
</ul>
<h2 style=3D"text-align: left;" id=3D"PRDUnifiedNavigation(deeplinkingR2fea=
turesinCX)-KeyDependencies">Key Dependencies</h2>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"fa246a6b-317f-49d8-bfd8-85b3645dc04e">R2 features will be=
 managed on legacy platform by the legacy delivery &amp; support teams.</li=
>
</ul>
<h1 style=3D"text-align: left;" id=3D"PRDUnifiedNavigation(deeplinkingR2fea=
turesinCX)-FeatureRequirements">Feature Requirements</h1>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"528e0d23-6af4-4cd5-a87a-c066e2a68ae9">Unified navigation =
experience should have none to limited changes when the features are rebuil=
t in the future.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"66625aa4-865f-4a5a-a31b-5004fb5c0618">Unified navigation =
should adapt to&nbsp; feature access &amp; permissions, have logical groupi=
ngs &amp; naming conventions.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"723980d4-f2cf-4bf7-9545-16a0ce98d735">Deep links to have =
branding and URL structure consistent with CX</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"10121726-d8b4-408b-8ad6-fcc196b6b2c9">Identify gaps in wo=
rkflow for Feature access/modification requests by clients for deep linked =
features. Determine whether these gaps can be addressed or require addition=
al features.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"c0e0f654-a9c3-4e0e-9476-baed5f889868">Identify gaps in wo=
rkflow for Feature access/modification request processing by NBIN teams for=
 deep linked features . Determine whether these gaps can be addressed or re=
quire additional features.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"d184dcce-fa42-414e-bccf-37879a410345">User experience, br=
anding etc for deep linked features should be consistent with CX user exper=
ience.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"185fbcb0-b43c-40c9-9f40-9e761d0cf3f2">For maintenance pur=
poses allow NBIN teams to access full legacy navigation.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"f8a98963-883b-4ed6-b43d-78394da498d8">Maintain session co=
ntinuity between CX and deep linked feature.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"b64b03ba-3dba-4d88-be6a-ea5f6cb1e8ae">State preservation =
(filters/search/ walk-me etc.)</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"71a15080-99f1-491b-b5af-97e3d7d9a540">Additional scenario=
s - white labeled firms. saved R2 bookmarks, external password preferences,=
 R2 links in email notifications, email id inconsistencies between CX &amp;=
 R2,&nbsp;</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"d90efa1f-2704-4906-93a5-e03bcd634e73">Additional impacts =
- operationalization with SAA teams, L&amp;D teams - walk-me walkthroughs i=
mpacts, other integrations besides R1</li>
</ul>
<h1 style=3D"text-align: left;" id=3D"PRDUnifiedNavigation(deeplinkingR2fea=
turesinCX)-OperationalImpact&amp;Considerations">Operational Impact &amp; C=
onsiderations</h1>
<p><br>
  &nbsp;Considerations for further discussions:</p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
 <table class=3D"relative-table wrapped confluenceTable" style=3D"width: 78=
.1007%;">
  <colgroup>
   <col style=3D"width: 2.60529%;">
   <col style=3D"width: 25.2444%;">
   <col style=3D"width: 40.7863%;">
   <col style=3D"width: 31.3563%;">
  </colgroup>
  <tbody class=3D"">
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p><br></p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p><strong>Issue</strong></p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p><strong>Details</strong></p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p><strong>Impacts/Examples</strong></p></td>
   </tr>
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>1</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Access will have to be maintained in both CX and R2 without profile=
 unification <strong><em>(Operational challenge)</em></strong></p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <ul>
      <li data-uuid=3D"9e309db9-3146-48b1-bbd2-3e9ba5ee688f">Deep linking e=
pic was envisioned as a one-time activity for feature onboarding &amp; comm=
unication.</li>
      <li data-uuid=3D"4549e1c2-6780-4c63-a161-fed6a3bf77d0">However, as F&=
amp;UM profile unification feature has been deprioritized the feature acces=
s will have to be maintained in two systems.</li>
     </ul></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <ul>
      <li data-uuid=3D"d7aebfb7-4b25-40bc-a2d1-4d308309a259">Ex: Access set=
tings for File Upload will have to be maintained separately in CX and R2 bo=
th</li>
      <li data-uuid=3D"c22e19d8-17df-47bd-9d57-d7ee3b5d86ec">Would user hav=
e to raise 2 requests to edit access to a deep linked feature ?</li>
     </ul></td>
   </tr>
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>2</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Deep linking feature having different permissions as compared to CX=
 profile &nbsp;<strong><em>(Operational challenge)</em></strong></p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <ul>
      <li data-uuid=3D"3ab6440c-8060-4bdd-b045-e1cae0bdfc86">Without F&amp;=
UM multi-firms feature in CX, deep linking will depend on the R2 permission=
s</li>
      <li data-uuid=3D"95b2ef17-1755-4f5a-bc57-b7895a761c7d">For subadvisor=
 &amp; parent-child firm users the permissions for deep linked feature will=
 be different from the remaining CX features</li>
     </ul></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <ul>
      <li data-uuid=3D"775d3ba3-6b28-4bc8-80f9-f00296a43109">Ex: User has d=
ifferent RR code assignment for deep linked File Upload feature v/s the Acc=
ounts module in CX</li>
     </ul></td>
   </tr>
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>3</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Hiding R2 navigation?</p>
     <p><strong><em>(User Experience)</em></strong></p>
     <p><br></p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <ul>
      <li data-uuid=3D"9509e84e-562c-488b-be5e-cda33adc23a2">One of our pri=
mary objectives for deep linking is to have a unified navigation</li>
      <li data-uuid=3D"1eb4ecb4-1053-4bd9-90f5-c06229ab5b25">However, multi=
 firm users would need access to R2 navigation enabled to have full feature=
 capability</li>
     </ul>
     <p><br></p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <ul>
      <li data-uuid=3D"fc5ea1f1-15fa-474f-814b-f7a10ab325c9">Ex: User needs=
 to access sub advisor clients under Accounts module</li>
     </ul></td>
   </tr>
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>4</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Users accessing R2 from restricted geographical locations</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <ul>
      <li data-uuid=3D"a7131985-93e8-41fe-9a3a-32e18352d6eb">This will not =
be addressed through deep linking and hence R2 access cannot be switched of=
f completely</li>
     </ul></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><br></td>
   </tr>
  </tbody>
 </table>
</div>
<p style=3D"text-align: left;"><br></p>
<p style=3D"text-align: left;"><span>Impact: Q4 Prioritization</span></p>
